entry("jet-matrix","three-obstacle-loewner-probe-jet-matrix","Three-obstacle Loewner probe jet matrix","For a capacity-2 chordal Loewner chain with real driver W and three obstacle-removal conformal maps h_i analytic near W with h_i'(W)>0, set u_i=h_i''(W)/h_i'(W) and c_i=h_i'''(W)/h_i'(W). The three-probe jet matrix J has row i equal to (u_i,c_i,u_i^2). This is algebraic independence of coefficient tests, not probabilistic independence of the obstacles.",["Three conformal maps analytic near the same driver","Positive map derivatives"],"definition")
entry("identification","localized-three-probe-loewner-characteristic-identification","DRAFT: local three-probe Loewner characteristic identification","Author-derived conditional result, pending independent review: let a capacity-2 chordal Loewner driver be a continuous semimartingale dW=mu dt+dN, with N a continuous local martingale and d<N>=v dt, v>=0 and locally integrable coefficients. Fix constant alpha>0. Before three fixed obstacles are hit, let h_i be their hydrodynamic maps, analytic at W with positive derivative. If each h_i'(W)^alpha is a local martingale on a common positive interval and the matrix with rows (h_i''/h_i',h_i'''/h_i',(h_i''/h_i')^2) is invertible for a.e. time there, then mu=0 and v=8/3 a.e. there and alpha=5/8. Global Brownian-driver/SLE identification additionally needs such intervals to cover all finite times.",["Continuous semimartingale driver with absolutely continuous drift/quadratic variation","Capacity normalization partial_t g=2/(g-W)","Common constant alpha>0","Reflected analytic conformal derivatives and local boundedness stops","Three local martingales over an interval","A.e. nondegenerate jet matrix","Globalization requires explicit coverage of all finite times"])
entry("stability","three-vertical-slit-probe-characteristic-stability","DRAFT: quantitative three-slit characteristic stability","At the three-slit initial jet matrix J=[[-1/2,-3/4,1/4],[1/2,-3/4,1/4],[-3/4,-9/16,9/16]], corresponding to slit locations/heights (1,1),(-1,1),(1,sqrt(3)), define normalized drift residuals e=J(mu,v/2-4/3,[1+v(alpha-1)]/2). If |e_i|<=epsilon, then |mu|<=2epsilon, |v-8/3|<=(52/9)epsilon and |1+v(alpha-1)|<=(40/3)epsilon. If v>=v_min>0, also |alpha-5/8|<=(31/(2v_min))epsilon. The inverse matrix norm in maximum absolute row sum is 20/3. These are fixed-configuration bounds, pending independent review, with no SAW residual estimate asserted.",["Exactly the displayed jet configuration","Residual normalized by alpha times the derivative-power process","Positive variance lower bound required for the exponent estimate","No global uniform jet control is assumed"])
entry("degeneracy","two-symmetric-slit-initial-tests-do-not-identify-loewner-coefficients","DRAFT: two symmetric initial probes leave a coefficient ambiguity","For the two symmetric vertical-slit jet rows (-1/2,-3/4,1/4) and (1/2,-3/4,1/4), the coefficient values mu=0,v=14/3,alpha=29/14 give theta=(mu,v/2-4/3,[1+v(alpha-1)]/2)=(0,1,3) and zero initial drift residual in both rows. The third row (-3/4,-9/16,9/16) gives residual 9/8. This exact pointwise algebra does not assert that those wrong coefficients make the first two processes martingales throughout an interval. Independent review is pending.",["Pointwise initial probes only","No claim of a process satisfying two full interval-martingale conditions"])
entry("gap","honeycomb-saw-three-probe-route-continuum-and-ensemble-gates","P0003 three-probe route: unproved continuum and ensemble inputs","The P0003 ledger source, Grimmett arXiv:2205.07318 Question 2.2, concerns uniform n-step honeycomb SAW from the origin under suitable rescaling. A related all-length critical boundary-to-boundary chordal conjecture is Duminil-Copin–Smirnov arXiv:1007.0575 Section 4 Conjecture 1. The w399 three-probe route proves only auxiliary conditional Loewner coefficient identification. Its hardest unproved input is convergence of localized random-domain SAW tail partition martingales to three derivative powers with one common positive exponent. Driver/filtration regularity, global probe coverage, curve convergence and transfer to the fixed-n ensemble are also unproved. Current openness is UNKNOWN; no full scaling-limit proof or novelty is claimed.",["Original fixed-n and working chordal ensembles are recorded separately","Finite identities and exact algebra checks do not discharge continuum inputs"])
